{
  "$schema_notes": [
    "External source registry for scrape_jobs.py. Edit this file to add/remove",
    "scrape targets without touching Python.",
    "",
    "Search role terms live in position_filter.json 'search_keyword_sets' (the",
    "  single source of truth). Reference a set from a source via",
    "  \"keyword_set\": \"<name>\". A 'keyword_sets' block here is rejected.",
    "",
    "sources: each entry needs \"name\", \"type\", \"region\". Then, by type:",
    "  - html / json_api : \"url\" (the page/endpoint to fetch)",
    "  - linkedin_api     : \"location\" + \"start\" + \"keyword_set\" (ref)",
    "  - google_proxy     : \"query\" (the Google 'q' string, with an optional",
    "                       \"{roles}\" slot filled from \"keyword_set\") + optional",
    "                       \"num\" (default 20)",
    "  Any source may instead supply an explicit \"url\" to override URL building.",
    "",
    "fallbacks: name -> [alternate urls] tried when a source returns no content."
  ],

